2. What Fiserv publicly documents about ACH

Fiserv’s current PEP+ material identifies prefunding as an ACH capability. 

More importantly, Fiserv has publicly documented an integration where PEP+ performs a real-time prefunding inquiry against the account system. In that integration, the downstream account system:

1. Receives the prefunding inquiry.
2. Validates the account.
3. Checks available balance.
4. Places a prefunding hold when configured to do so.
5. Returns an availability/result response.
6. Releases prefunding holds during subsequent ACH processing. 

That is very close to the workflow you’ve been describing:

Fiserv / ACH Processing
        │
        │ Prefund Request
        ▼
Bank Account System
        │
        ├── Validate account
        ├── Check available funds
        ├── Earmark / Hold
        │
        ▼
     Response
        │
        ▼
Fiserv / ACH Processing

So your pre-fund reservation application is conceptually sound, but we should distinguish the NACHA settlement file from the internal/vendor-to-bank prefunding interface.

