3. Standard NACHA file structure

For your parser, I would start with this canonical model.

FILE
│
├── FILE HEADER
│
├── BATCH 1
│   ├── BATCH HEADER
│   ├── ENTRY 1
│   │   └── ADDENDA
│   ├── ENTRY 2
│   ├── ENTRY 3
│   └── BATCH CONTROL
│
├── BATCH 2
│   ├── BATCH HEADER
│   ├── ENTRY 1
│   ├── ENTRY 2
│   └── BATCH CONTROL
│
└── FILE CONTROL

Nacha explicitly describes the file, batch and transaction hierarchy and the corresponding header/control records. 

