17. Important distinction: Refund vs Return

This is very important for your requirements.

A refund is generally a new payment/credit transaction intended to send money back to someone.

An ACH return is the return of an existing ACH entry under the ACH return framework.

They are not interchangeable.

So if Fiserv is sending:

“Please refund $250 to customer account XYZ”

that is different from:

“Return the previously received ACH entry because of R01/R02/etc.”

Your application should therefore have separate business models:

ACH Refund Request

and:

ACH Return

even though both may ultimately use NACHA records.

